description: TabGen project overview and conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

TabGen: song -> guitar chords (Phase 1), tabs (Phase 2), play-along check (Phase 3). Personal, local-first (macOS / Apple Silicon), free, no cloud services.

Layout
- `workers/analysis/tabgen_analysis/` — Python pipeline. One module per stage in `stages/` (decode, separate, beats, structure, chords, key, post). Each stage is cached per audio hash under `data/tracks/<hash>/stages/<model-key>.json`; change a stage's MODEL_KEY when its model/settings change. `pipeline.py` orchestrates; bump `PIPELINE_VERSION` in `config.py` when the output JSON changes.
- `apps/api/tabgen_api/` — FastAPI + in-process single-thread job queue; serves `apps/web/dist` at `/`.
- `apps/web/` — React + Vite + TS. Chord logic (Harte parsing, transpose, capo, simplify) is pure TS in `src/music/chords.ts` with vitest tests; it mirrors `tabgen_analysis/chord_label.py`.
- A separate polished UI lives under `design/` (other branch) — don't edit it from pipeline work.

Models (keep swappable; see README licenses): Beat This! (beats), all-in-one-infer (sections, reuses our stems), lv-chordia (chords, behind `ChordRecognizer` in `stages/chords.py`), S-KEY (key), Demucs htdemucs_6s (stems). Do not add madmom NC models, Essentia, Chordino, BTC, Rubber Band, or other GPL/AGPL/NC components.

UI text: Turkish first, English second, all strings in `apps/web/src/i18n.tsx`.

Commands: `./scripts/setup.sh`, `./scripts/run.sh`, `./scripts/dev.sh`, `cd apps/web && npx vitest run`, `pytest workers/analysis/tests`.
